cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the companion paper."
title: "RED-2400 Replication Toolkit"
abstract: >
  Reproducible filter-precision auditing of algorithmic decentralized-exchange
  trading systems against the RED-2400 public benchmark dataset. Implements the
  five-tier outcome-classification rule with a canonical event identity model
  (P11 event_id = sha256("event|" + mint + "|" + rejectTs_utc_ms + "|" + rejectReason)),
  per-filter audit reporting, aggregate save-to-miss ratios under conservative
  and combined interpretations, and the matched-comparison early-death
  validation from Kamat (2026). v2 supersedes v1.0.0's mint-collapse defect
  in which the classifier pooled outcome rows by mint rather than by
  rejection event.
type: software
version: "2.0.1"
# date-released is the actual push date of the v2.0.1 tag on origin
# (see JOSS_REPAIR_2026-09-15/PHASE6_RELEASE_LOG.md § 4).
date-released: "2026-09-15"
license: MIT
